<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">National Liberation Front (South Yemen)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1963">1963</a>–<a href="/years/1978">1978</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-liberation-front-algeria">National Liberation Front</a> was a Marxist-leaning nationalist movement that fought British rule in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aden">Aden</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorates</a> from 1963. In 1967 it defeated its rival <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/front-for-the-liberation-of-occupied-south-yemen">FLOSY</a>, overthrew the sultans and sheikhs of the Federation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-arabia">South Arabia</a>, and proclaimed the People's Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-yemen">South Yemen</a> when the British withdrew in November. It later became the core of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemeni-socialist-party">Yemeni Socialist Party</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/national-liberation-front-south-yemen.jpg" alt="National Liberation Front (South Yemen)" width="320" height="391" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Emblem_of_the_National_Liberation_Front_(South_Yemen).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
